						<p class=3D"PaperBody">When discussing programming languages, people =
often position R and SAS as competitors. If you primarily program in R and =
are new to SAS=E2=80=94or vice versa=E2=80=94you might be surprised by how =
many ways you can combine the strengths of both languages. The newest and a=
rguably most seamless way to integrate R with SAS is the R procedure (PROC =
R) that became available in SAS Viya 2026.03.</p>
<p class=3D"PaperBody">&nbsp;</p>
<p>Users can easily pass data sets from SAS to R and back using the followi=
ng functions:</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>sd2df or sasdata2dataframe:</strong> exports a SAS data set to a=
 local R data frame using the haven package. Note that starting in SAS Viya=
 2026.05, the following two syntax options will be available.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span>df &lt;- sd2df("sashelp.cars")</span></p>
<p><span>df &lt;- sd2df("cars", "sashelp")</span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>df2sd of dataframe2sasdata:</strong> transfers an R data frame t=
o a SAS data set. Note that starting in SAS Viya 2026.05, the following two=
 syntax options will be available.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span>df2sd(df, "work.cars_r")</span></p>
<p><span>df2sd(df, "cars_r", "work")</span></p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>The following example converts SASHELP.CARS to an R data frame and use=
s the <span>filter()</span> function from the tidyverse collection of packa=
ges in R to only keep Audi vehicles. Then, the filtered data frame is conve=
rted to a SAS table called AUDI stored in the WORK library. Finally, we pri=
nt the newly created table with a PROC PRINT step.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>
<div>
<pre class=3D"  language-sas"><code class=3D"  language-sas"><span class=3D=
"token step keyword">proc r</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">;</span=
>=20
    submit<span class=3D"token punctuation">;</span>
    <span class=3D"token function keyword">library</span><span class=3D"tok=
en punctuation">(</span>tidyverse<span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span>
    carsdf <span class=3D"token operator">&lt;</span><span class=3D"token o=
perator">-</span> <span class=3D"token function keyword">sd2df</span><span =
class=3D"token punctuation">(</span><span class=3D"token string">"sashelp.c=
ars"</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span>
    carsAudi <span class=3D"token operator">&lt;</span><span class=3D"token=
 operator">-</span> carsdf <span class=3D"token punctuation">%</span><span =
class=3D"token operator">&gt;</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">%</sp=
an> <span class=3D"token function keyword">filter</span><span class=3D"toke=
n punctuation">(</span>Make <span class=3D"token operator">=3D</span><span =
class=3D"token operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"token string">"Audi"</sp=
an><span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span>
    <span class=3D"token function keyword">df2sd</span><span class=3D"token=
 punctuation">(</span>carsAudi<span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span> <s=
pan class=3D"token string">"work.audi"</span><span class=3D"token punctuati=
on">)</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">;</span>
    endsubmit<span class=3D"token punctuation">;</span>
<span class=3D"token step keyword">run</span><span class=3D"token punctuati=
on">;</span>

<span class=3D"token step keyword">proc print</span> <span class=3D"token p=
roc-args"><span class=3D"token arg keyword">data</span><span class=3D"token=
 operator">=3D</span><span class=3D"token arg-value">work.audi</span><span =
class=3D"token punctuation">;</span></span>
<span class=3D"token step keyword">run</span><span class=3D"token punctuati=
on">;</span>
</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
